dismissed_items.source_en:
Idly waiting was not Donna's style. Even before summer arrived, she had already gathered quite a bit of information at the Trekker Camp in Sailstead.

Some said the person might be a young Trekker in their early twenties who loved Sailstead's beaches and came here every summer;
some said it might be a middle-aged Trekker around forty who had once lost something important while exploring that Monolith and returned every summer to search for it;
others said the recipient might be a female Trekker, memorable because she was a redhead who showed up every summer.
...

So what kind of person would the recipient turn out to be?

